# Committed template — IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md task 5.5. Copy to `.env`
# (gitignored, never committed) and fill in real values.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are bundled directly into the client at build
# time — anyone can read them from the compiled app. Only put something
# here with that prefix if it's *meant* to be public. The Supabase anon/
# publishable key is: Supabase's own design protects data via Row Level
# Security policies (supabase/migrations/0001_initial_schema.sql), not by
# keeping this key secret. Nothing else in this project should ever use
# the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix — the Groq API key, when it's wired in
# (macro-stage 9), stays backend-only, never in this file.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
